{'symbol': 'BA', 'date': '2020-08-01 22:30:00', 'title': 'Icelandair Says Negotiations With Stakeholders To Initiate Offering Of New Shares In Final Stages', 'text': 'ICELANDAIR GROUP  - NEGOTIATING WITH STAKEHOLDERS IN ORDER TO BE ABLE TO INITIATE OFFERING OF NEW SHARES AND COMPLETE A FINANCIAL RESTRUCTURING OF CO.NEGOTIATIONS ARE IN FINAL STAGES.FULLY DOCUMENTED AGREEMENTS HAVE BEEN COMPLETED WITH MAJORITY OF CREDITORS.ICELANDAIR GROUP - NEGOTIATIONS WITH REMAINING CREDITORS ARE AT AN ADVANCED STAGE AND FINAL AGREEMENTS ARE EXPECTED TO BE FULLY DOCUMENTED NEXT WEEK.NEGOTIATIONS WITH CREDITORS HAVE FOCUSED ON RESTRUCTURING CASH OUTFLOWS TO MATCH EXPECTED FUTURE CASH INFLOWS.ICELANDAIR- CO HAS ALREADY COMPLETED LONG-TERM COLLECTIVE-BARGAINING AGREEMENTS WITH PILOT, CABIN CREW, AND AIRCRAFT MAINTENANCE UNIONS.ICELANDAIR- SEES RECEIVING FURTHER COMPENSATION FOR LOSS DUE TO GROUNDING, CHANGES WILL BE MADE TO DELIVERY SCHEDULE OF FUTURE BOEING 737-MAX ORDERS.'}
{'symbol': 'CAT', 'date': '2020-08-01 08:30:00', 'title': 'Caterpillar Reports Q2 Earnings Per Share $0.84', 'text': "CATERPILLAR REPORTS SECOND-QUARTER 2020 RESULTS.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.84.Q2 SALES $10 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $9.38 BILLION.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.64 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.NOT PROVIDING A FINANCIAL OUTLOOK FOR 2020 AT THIS TIME..FINANCIAL RESULTS FOR REMAINDER OF 2020 WILL BE IMPACTED BY CONTINUED GLOBAL ECONOMIC UNCERTAINTY DUE TO COVID-19 PANDEMIC.AS OF MID-JULY 2020, GLOBALLY AND ACROSS 3 PRIMARY SEGMENTS, NEARLY ALL PRIMARY PRODUCTION FACILITIES CONTINUED TO OPERATE.CATERPILLAR - DEALERS DECREASED MACHINE AND ENGINE INVENTORIES ABOUT $1.4 BILLION DURING Q2 2020, COMPARED WITH INCREASE OF ABOUT $500 MILLION DURING Q2 2019.EXPENSE FOR CORPORATE ITEMS AND ELIMINATIONS WAS $580 MILLION IN Q2 OF 2020, AN INCREASE OF $89 MILLION FROM Q2 OF 2019.DECLINE IN QTRLY SALES WAS DUE TO LOWER SALES VOLUME DRIVEN BY LOWER END-USER DEMAND AND IMPACT FROM CHANGES IN DEALER INVENTORIES.AT THE END OF Q2, PAST DUES AT CAT FINANCIAL WERE 3.74%, VERSUS 3.38% AT THE END OF Q2 OF 2019.AS OF JUNE 30, CAT FINANCIAL'S ALLOWANCE FOR CREDIT LOSSES TOTALED $515 MILLION, VERSUS $457 MILLION AT MARCH 31."}
{'symbol': 'CVX', 'date': '2020-08-01 08:30:00', 'title': 'Chevron Announces Q2 Loss Per Share $4.44', 'text': 'CHEVRON ANNOUNCES SECOND QUARTER 2020 RESULTS.Q2 LOSS PER SHARE $4.44.Q2 SALES $16 BILLION VERSUS $36 BILLION.Q2 ADJUSTED LOSS PER SHARE $1.59.Q2 REVENUE ESTIMATE $22.1 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $-0.92 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY RESULTS  INCLUDES NON-CASH NET CHARGES OF $5.2 BILLION AND A $310 MILLION ASSET SALE GAIN.WORLDWIDE NET OIL-EQUIVALENT PRODUCTION WAS 2.99 MILLION BARRELS PER DAY IN Q2 2020, A DECREASE OF 3 PERCENT FROM A YEAR AGO.INTERNATIONAL DOWNSTREAM OPERATIONS REPORTED A LOSS OF $22 MILLION IN Q2 2020, COMPARED WITH EARNINGS OF $264 MILLION A YEAR EARLIER.U.S. UPSTREAM OPERATIONS REPORTED A LOSS OF $2.1 BILLION IN Q2 2020, COMPARED WITH EARNINGS OF $896 MILLION A YEAR EARLIER.INTERNATIONAL REFINERY CRUDE OIL INPUT OF 589,000 BARRELS PER DAY IN Q2 2020 DECREASED 2 PERCENT FROM YEAR-AGO PERIOD.U.S. DOWNSTREAM OPERATIONS REPORTED A LOSS OF $988 MILLION IN Q2 2020, COMPARED WITH EARNINGS OF $465 MILLION A YEAR EARLIER.U.S. NET OIL-EQUIVALENT PRODUCTION OF 991,000 BARRELS PER DAY IN Q2 2020 WAS UP 93,000 BARRELS PER DAY FROM A YEAR EARLIER.INCLUDED IN CURRENT QUARTER WERE IMPAIRMENTS AND OTHER NET CHARGES OF $1.8 BILLION.U.S. REFINERY CRUDE OIL INPUT IN Q2 2020 DECREASED 39% TO 581,000 BARRELS PER DAY FROM YEAR-AGO PERIOD.INTERNATIONAL UPSTREAM OPERATIONS REPORTED A LOSS OF $4.0 BILLION IN Q2 2020, COMPARED WITH EARNINGS OF $2.6 BILLION A YEAR AGO.'}
